// https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geomantic_figures#The_geomantic_figures

// `meaning` and `meanings` (the figure in each house): the Golden Dawn's table
// as Crowley printed it in "A Handbook of Geomancy", The Equinox I(2), 1909,
// pp. 154-156 (public domain; archive.org crowley-equinox_202110, file "The
// Equinox Vol. 1, No. 2", leaves n158-n160), read from the page images (plan
// 075). Editorial changes, nothing else: abbreviations spelled out (esp.,
// exc., V., Gd., Med., Cf., figs., &); "evil" and "ill" read "unfavourable",
// or "bad" in the paired formulas of Caput and Cauda Draconis, Conjunctio,
// Populus and Rubeus; each entry ends with a full stop. Plan 075 lists every
// edited cell. `translation`: the Latin names' plain English.

